    <section class="cl-hero">
      <h1>Changelog</h1>
      <p class="lede">What changed in each version of bunnyhop.lol, newest first. The current version is <b>v0.0.15 alpha</b>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="cl-list" aria-label="Versions">
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.15"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.15">v0.0.15</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-10">10 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Supporting opens, favorite maps and !showtriggers</h3><ul><li>Supporting bunnyhop.lol is open: a one-time payment of $5 or more, any amount you like, from Support at the bottom of the main menu. It unlocks all three supporter sets and both supporter knives, a heart next to your name, a name colour and effect, a spot in a full server and a place in Top supporters. Sign in with Discord or email first so it stays with your account. The game stays free, and nothing you can buy helps you play.</li><li>The Support page fits on one screen: every supporter item is on the right, grouped by set, to try on, and Top supporters has its own tab.</li><li>Favorite maps: star a map by its name in the map list or beside Play, then switch All maps to Favorites to see just those. Your stars follow your account to any device.</li><li>!showtriggers and !showclips show a map's teleports, boosters and other triggers, and its player clips and invisible walls; !triggers picks which kinds. Runs with them on count as usual.</li><li>Your USP's silencer stays as it was when you restart, and your gun is already in your hand, ready to shoot.</li><li>Chat shows your cursor: press Y (or U) and you can scroll back through the chat with the mouse wheel while you type. The game keeps going underneath, and Enter, Esc or a click on the game puts you straight back in.</li><li>No more &#34;too many submissions&#34;: grind a short map as much as you like, every finish counts.</li><li>#1 on the Auto-strafe rank now earns the Style Champion title, like #1 in any other style. Auto-strafe keeps its own leaderboards and rank.</li><li>New players get Learn to bhop right on the main menu for their first two days, until they finish it.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.14"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.14">v0.0.14</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-09">9 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>64 new maps, the Hermes map and supporter sets</h3><ul><li>63 new maps. 49 are the maps people clear most on the big CS:GO servers, in their CS:S versions; 14 come straight from CS:GO (bhop_easystrafe_1, borders, sp_v3, noodles_v2, topbhop_v1, mixempire and more); and kz_bhop_essence, which you asked for in Discord. Short ones to start with: bhop_3_easy, bhop_xcsource, bhop_royal, bhop_coal_mines_css and bhop_passionlessly. For a longer run, try bhop_reportal or bhop_nup2_css.</li><li>bhop_lol_hermes, a new original map: a T3 run of two minutes or more through seven themed sections, with launch pads, spinning gears and a surf slide, up to a city in the clouds.</li><li>Staff badges: a small shield next to the name of moderators (green), admins (blue) and the developer (gold), on the leaderboards, profiles, in chat and above players in servers, so you can always tell who's staff.</li><li>Your !usp or !glock stays with you when you restart.</li><li>Supporting bunnyhop.lol opens soon: a one-time payment of $5 or more, for three thank-you sets of cosmetics. The game stays free. Support, at the bottom of the main menu, lets you try them all on now.</li><li>Three supporter sets: Geode (four gems orbiting your head, a crystal halo, a circlet and three animated finishes), High Roller (a dealer's visor, lucky coins, a gold-leaf finish) and Borealis (an aurora ribbon and an aurora finish), each with its colourway, gloves, trail, ghost colour, card frame and background. Supporters also get a badge next to their name, a name colour and effect (glow, gradient or shine), a spot in a full server, and a place in Top supporters and on the About page they can opt out of.</li><li>Two supporter knives: the Thornback, a big sawback bayonet you toss and catch, and the Thistle, a slim bayonet that spins round your finger.</li><li>Main menu is back at the bottom of the pause menu, in red so it's easy to find; Backspace also takes you there, and you can bind a key for it in Settings, Keys to leave straight from the game.</li><li>Something out there has wings.</li><li>bhop_tesquo_v2's neon boosters work: stand on a booster platform, shoot it with the Glock the stage gives you and jump to fly up. Shots and knife hits now reach physics boxes like in CS:S.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.13"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.13">v0.0.13</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-08">8 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Potato mode, six new songs and a pause menu that fits</h3><ul><li>bhop_2easy's teleports to the next stage now cover the back of each end room, wall to wall, so you can't jump over them or walk past them any more, and the blue trails that mark them in CS:S spin around them again (other maps' spinning trails show up too).</li><li>Maps lit by named or flickering lights aren't dark anymore: bhop_cutekittenz past its start room, kz_bhop_indiana's tunnels, bhop_legenda_v2, bhop_catalyst_fix and a few others are now lit like in CS:S.</li><li>Fixed the view sometimes snapping to the floor or somewhere else in Chrome, Edge and Opera on Windows: the mouse filter now catches the browser's fake jumps when they come in pairs or during fast strafes, and real flicks still go through.</li><li>Auto-strafe: hold A or D in the air to strafe yourself (for surf ramps), and W now moves you forward in the air while the game keeps strafing for you.</li><li>Potato mode in Settings, Graphics: flat colours like dev textures, plain water and sky, for laptops and slow GPUs. Maps with a lot of water (arcane, advi_new, crash_egypt, bkz_goldbhop) also run faster for everyone, with no change in how they look.</li><li>Six new songs in the in-game playlist (P skips to the next one).</li><li>The pause menu fits on laptop screens without scrolling: Main menu is a button at the top, and Leaderboard, Style, Replays, On screen and Help are tabs above the panel on the right.</li><li>The profile's Collection tab is gone: your items are in Loadout and Edit card, and Edit card, Badges now also lists the achievements you haven't earned yet, with your progress.</li><li>Profile and Loadout in the menus no longer show new-unlock hints, and your profile no longer opens with a &#34;Since your last visit&#34; card. Unlocks still get their card when they happen, and new items keep a dot until you look at them.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.12"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.12">v0.0.12</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-08">8 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Weapon commands, the USP silencer, solo chat and !ssj</h3><ul><li>Chat commands work in single player too: press Y and type !r, !b, !setstart, !clearstart and the rest, like in online servers. !help lists them, and the up arrow brings back what you typed before (in servers too).</li><li>Weapon commands like on bhop servers: !usp, !glock and !knife (or 5 and 6) replace the gun in that slot and draw it. !gun &#60;name&#62; or !guns (7) gets any of our guns in practice mode and on unranked maps; ranked runs stick to the USP, Glock and knife.</li><li>The USP has its silencer: right-click screws it on or off, which takes about 3 seconds like in CS:S. It's quieter with it on, and other players in your server see it.</li><li>Right-click now does what Mouse 2 is bound to (the knife's stab, the silencer). Until now the middle button did. If you bound right-click or the middle button to something yourself, it stays on the same button.</li><li>bhop_monster_jam's buttons break their walls again, so the main track can be finished, and bhop_hive's breakable walls work the same way. Walls that break, switch off or get removed now disappear from view too, and come back when the map brings them back.</li><li>A better !help: a few short lines with your own keys, !help practice (or styles, bhop, keys) explains one thing, and the pause menu has a Help tab. The names you know from bhop servers work too (!noclip, !cp, !tele, !n, !sw, !hsw, !wr, !pb), and a mistyped command suggests the closest one.</li><li>!ssj: your speed, gain, sync and strafes on the 6th jump (or every jump, or every 6th) as a line in chat, counted the way bhop servers' SSJ plugin counts them. Type !ssj or go to Settings, HUD, Jump stats to turn it on and pick what it shows; the Jump stats element puts the same numbers on your HUD and in replays.</li><li>New players start a map looking at it, with one line: click to start. Esc still opens the menu. The tutorial's ending plays one thing at a time now, and the bunny no longer covers the words.</li><li>Finishing the intro is saved properly: some players were shown it again on another device.</li><li>The first-visit intro is shorter: the strafing drill is gone, and the tutorial teaches it in the map instead.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.11"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.11">v0.0.11</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-07">7 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Start points, hide UI, guns in servers and Discord feeds</h3><ul><li>Hide UI for recording clips: press F1 in game, while spectating or in a replay and only the game is left, with your speed and keys if you want them (Settings, HUD, Hide UI). In game it stays hidden until you press F1 again; Esc still opens the pause menu. In replays it's also a button next to HUD, and Esc brings the controls back.</li><li>Start points: stand still anywhere in a start zone and press 4 (or type !setstart in a server), and restarts put you on that spot, facing the way you were. Clear start point (!clearstart) goes back to the usual spot. Each map and bonus keeps its own, and runs from them count like any other.</li><li>Boosting the bunnyhop.lol Discord server puts a pink gem next to your name on the leaderboards, your profile and in online rooms. Link Discord to your account and it shows up on its own; it goes away when the boost ends. Edit card, Badges has a switch to hide it.</li><li>Items you own say how you got them in the Loadout, the Collection and Edit card, with the date and the map when a run earned them.</li><li>In online rooms you now see the gun other players are holding, and hear and see their shots.</li><li>Guns sit lower and further out on the right, the left hand holds the rifles and shotguns from underneath instead of a big sleeve coming up the middle of the screen, and the bottom-right corner shows the rounds left in the clip instead of the gun's name (Ammo in the HUD layout).</li><li>The boost pads on bhop_badges and bhop_badges_mini work like in CS:S: the first shot at a pad boosts you, and the Glock's burst fires once per click.</li><li>If your account is linked to Discord and you're in the bunnyhop.lol server, ┃levels posts a card with your avatar and frame when you reach level 5, 10, 20, 30 or 50, clear your first T4, T5 or T6 map, or finish 100 maps.</li><li>Snipes: when someone takes your world record and you're in the Discord server, ┃snipes posts it with the replay and pings you. /snipes or the button in ┃roles turns the pings off.</li><li>Every Monday the Discord server names a Player of the Week: whoever set the most world records that week that still stand. They get the Player of the Week role until the next one.</li><li>┃servers in the Discord server shows who's playing in each online server, with a Join button.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.10"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.10">v0.0.10</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-07">7 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>77 new maps, a new map list, practice mode and guns</h3><ul><li>77 new maps, 34 of them T1 or T2. For getting started there's bhop_atom, bhop_lm, bhop_dom, bhop_kitum, bhop_zentic, bhop_emevaelx3 and bhop_blue_shade_fix; for later, bhop_colour, bhop_dragon_fix, bhop_enigma, bhop_hangtime2_fix and bhop_futile.</li><li>Play has a new map list. Pick a map and its leaderboard is right there: the top times, the world record and your own time and rank, without loading the map. Full leaderboard opens the whole board.</li><li>Styles are one switch at the top of the map list, each by its full name, with its rule beside it. The style you pick there is the one for the times in the list, the leaderboard you're looking at and the run you start.</li><li>Every map in the list shows its tier, your PB, the world record, a WR mark on the records you hold, and Played on maps you haven't finished yet. Maps with bonus tracks say how many.</li><li>Search, a tier filter, the map sets and six ways to sort: popular, easiest first, newest, name, not played yet and unfinished. The arrow keys move through the list, Enter plays, / jumps to the search and F3 switches style.</li><li>Unranked maps say so in the list and where their leaderboard would be, instead of showing an empty board.</li><li>The tutorial moved from the main menu to the top of the map list, with your lessons, your best time and the final course's leaderboard. If you don't need it, Hide tutorial takes it off the list and the pause menu (it's also in Settings, Account). Tutorial, under the main menu, always opens it.</li><li>The main menu has one panel on the right now: a map to play and three to try next. Recent records and the stats tiles are gone from it, and Play online is a menu item like the others.</li><li>On a phone the map list fits the screen: tap a map to see its leaderboard. You still need a computer to play.</li><li>Practice mode, in the pause menu: fly through the map with noclip (Z), save checkpoints (C) and teleport back to them (X). A teleport gives you back the time and speed you had. Nothing you do in practice is submitted or saved as a PB, and leaving it puts you back at the start. It's for solo play.</li><li>Turn with the arrow keys in practice mode, like +left and +right in CS:S. You can rebind them in Settings, Keys, Practice.</li><li>Third person (T) is off during a timed run, so a stray press can't turn your run into practice. It works as before in the start zone, after you finish and in practice mode.</li><li>Z no longer opens the zone editor. It's the noclip key in practice mode now.</li><li>Guns work on the maps that hand them out. On bhop_badges and bhop_badges_mini you pick a gun up from its stand and shoot the pads to be pushed up or sideways; fire again just as each push runs out to keep climbing. 1, 2 and 3 pick a slot, Q goes back to your last weapon and G drops the gun you hold. They're in Settings, Keys, Weapons. bhop_badges and bhop_badges_mini are ranked again.</li><li>Guns a map gives you are our own: the Thumper burst pistol, the Cottontail, the heavy Jackrabbit, the Broadfork pump shotgun, the Hedgerow auto shotgun, the Seed Drill, which feeds from a pea pod, the Furrow rifle and the Beanpole sniper with its sliding bolt. Each has its own sounds, recoil, reload and an inspect on F, held in your gloves, and your bunny holds it in third person.</li><li>Guns lie on the floor where the map puts them and where you drop them, and replays show them too, along with the gun in your bunny's hand.</li><li>bhop_2flocci2furious's stepping tiles hold you now, as they do in CS:S; before, you fell through them. A few other maps with the same kind of tile (bhop_thc_island, bhop_ivy_final and some others) get them too. Thanks to Blackmale42 for the report.</li><li>Long runs save. A run can be up to 4 hours now; before, a run of about an hour was too big to upload and was lost. If a long run of yours was refused before this update and it's still your PB on that map in this browser, it's sent again the next time you open the game, and you'll get a message when it's verified.</li><li>If an upload fails because of the connection or because you closed the tab, the run is kept in your browser and sent again once. The end-of-run card says so instead of only saying the leaderboard is offline.</li><li>Runs are checked faster: most verdicts come a couple of seconds sooner, and the card picks them up sooner too. Long runs are checked separately, so they no longer hold up anyone else's, and the card shows how far along the check is.</li><li>Player cards show how long you've played instead of time on the clock. It counts time spent playing a map, practice and online servers included, and starts from an estimate based on the runs you've uploaded. Cards also no longer say whether an account signed in with Discord or email. Guests still show as guest.</li><li>Clocked In and Overtime now count the hours you play, not just time on the clock in finished runs. If you already have the hours, they unlock with your next finished run.</li><li>TikTok and X creators get a creator mark too, next to the YouTube and Twitch ones.</li><li>Auto-strafe: hold S in the air to stop the automatic strafing and slow down, so you can drop into small holes. Your own A and D work while you hold it.</li><li>Tiers are fixed on 40 maps. kz_bhop_yonkoma and kz_bhop_indiana were listed as T1 and are T4 now, kz_bhop_benchmark is T5, and the rest moved one tier to match what most servers use. Points and ranks are worked out again with the new tiers.</li><li>bhop_arcane_v2 replaces bhop_arcane_v1. It's the version most servers run: the same map without the random pushes on the ice platforms.</li><li>Duplicate copies of maps are gone from the list: bhop_mp_stairs_dev, bhop_mp_stairs_hq, bhop_larena_nodoors, bhop_null, bhop_aztec_fixed, bhop_fps_max and bhop_frost_bite_v1a. Your times on them stay on your profile, but they no longer give points.</li><li>Maps download in about half the size, so they load faster.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.9"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.9">v0.0.9</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-07">7 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>A new Loadout, automatic Discord rewards and better ladders</h3><ul><li>The Loadout has everything you wear in the game now: knife, finish, gloves, your bunny's colourway, your ghost and its trail. Hover anything to see it on your hands, your bunny or your ghost, click to put it on.</li><li>Your profile card is edited on the card itself. Press Edit card under it and pick a background, frame, title, badges or links. The Customise tab is gone.</li><li>Discord rewards are automatic. Link Discord and you get Blurple if you're in the bunnyhop.lol server, and the Afterglow set if you boost it. If you join later it shows up within the hour, a new boost within a few hours. No more Check membership button.</li><li>You can answer our replies to your feedback. Open the reply in your Inbox and write back under it. It goes into the same conversation, so there's no need to send a new report.</li><li>Your knife works on the map now: left click swings, right click stabs, like in CS:S. Hit a button that's meant to be shot and it presses. On bhop_hive, knife the keypad next to the first door and the door opens, so the map can be finished. Thanks to wik for the report.</li><li>Ladders climb like in CS:S. Holding W goes straight up instead of drifting sideways off the ladder, ducking climbs slower, and you can hang still. bhop_monster_jam's narrow ladders can be climbed now. Thanks to Frosty_Leaper for the report.</li><li>Water that a map raises and lowers is real water now: you can swim in it instead of falling through. On bhop_lost_world, turn the valve in the lab (press E) and the tank floods. bhop_crash_egypt's tide rises and falls again, and the pools on bh_aztec, bhop_algebradude, bhop_militia_v2, bhop_runbhopper_v2 and other maps can be swum in.</li><li>Runs set before this update keep their times and replays.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.8"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.8">v0.0.8</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-06">6 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>The Discord, fair play and a tutorial that finishes</h3><ul><li>bunnyhop.lol has a Discord: Join the Discord is on the home screen, the About page and in What's new. You can also sign in with Discord now. In the server, linked players get roles for their level, crown and world records, pick a name colour, and can ask the bot for /leaderboard, /wr, /pb and /profile.</li><li>Link Discord to your account (click your name, then Link Discord) and the Sport · Blurple gloves are yours.</li><li>Join the bunnyhop.lol Discord server, then press Check membership (Profile → Customise → Colourway) for the Blurple bunny colourway. Boosting the server gets you the Afterglow set: Moto · Afterglow gloves, the Afterglow colourway and trail, and a Server booster mark on your profile while you boost. Everything you earn stays yours, even if you leave the server or stop boosting.</li><li>Linked Discord? You can use your Discord avatar as your bunnyhop.lol avatar: click your name and turn on Use my Discord avatar, right under Discord. It shows on your profile and the leaderboards instead of your letter. It's off unless you turn it on, and you can turn it off any time.</li><li>Played bunnyhop.lol before this update? You get the Early Hopper achievement and title. Thanks for being here early.</li><li>Learn to bhop: finishing the final course now counts. Coming in from the lessons, the finish said &#34;practice run (third person)&#34; and the home screen stayed on &#34;3 of 4 lessons done&#34;. Now you arrive on the course's start pad, and your time is submitted like any other run.</li><li>The tutorial's final course has a leaderboard. When you finish you see the top 10, your place and the next time to beat. Leaderboard next to Learn to bhop on the home screen shows the whole board. It doesn't give rank points.</li><li>When you unlock something, its card now shows a little 3D model of it instead of a flat icon: your new gloves, finish or knife turning in the light, a medal for an achievement, a nameplate for a title, a ribbon for a trail. With reduced motion turned on it stays still.</li><li>Runs are now checked more closely for scripted or automated input. Runs that a person couldn't have played are rejected automatically, and others may be looked at by a moderator. If you think one of your runs was rejected by mistake, tell us through Feedback in the game.</li><li>Moderators are here: they show with a Mod tag in chat, on the scoreboard and on player cards. We're looking for more: apply in the game through Feedback (pick Moderator application), and come say hi in the Discord.</li><li>If a new version comes out while you have the game open, opening a menu or panel that hadn't been loaded yet no longer fails: the game reloads into the new version (never during a run), or tells you to.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.7"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.7">v0.0.7</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-06">6 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Fairness, creators and reliability</h3><ul><li>When a new version of bunnyhop.lol comes out while you have the game open, a quiet note says so with a Reload button. It only shows in the menus (or tells you to press Esc right after a run), never interrupts a run, and reloading brings you back to the same map and style. A run you just finished is uploaded first.</li><li>Start zones now work like bhoptimer. Your timer starts from the ground inside the start zone: walk out, jump, or drop off a ledge inside it, and a jump counts from takeoff. Flying through the zone in the air no longer starts a run, so mid-air exits at a free 290 u/s and ledge starts are gone. To reset in the zone, land and stand for a moment (or press R). Thanks to Those who So for the report.</li><li>Runs set before this update keep their times and replays.</li><li>Verified players now have a blue check next to their name, and YouTube and Twitch creators a small creator mark: in server chat, on the scoreboard and name tags, on leaderboards and ranks, on profiles and in profile link previews. Only bunnyhop.lol hands them out, so nobody can fake one.</li><li>Put your YouTube, Twitch, X and TikTok on your profile: Profile → Customise → Links. Just your handle (or paste a link to your page); links only ever go to that site. They stay hidden until you turn on Show on my profile.</li><li>The main menu fits on shorter screens (a 720p screen, or 1080p with display scaling) instead of cutting off the bottom items.</li><li>Runs on the biggest maps, like bhop_miku_v2 and bhop_dimensions, now verify on the first try, and a run can no longer sit on &#34;waiting for verification&#34; for hours: anything stuck is picked up again within minutes. If a run can't be verified because of a problem on our side, the end-of-run card says so instead of calling it rejected.</li><li>New to bhop? Learn to bhop is open to everyone: a short hands-on course from the home screen that teaches jumping, strafing and gaining speed, ending in a small graduation run.</li><li>Runs with key presses no human can make (like switching strafe keys every single tick) are now rejected automatically, and banned players can't submit runs. Cheated records on bhop_bfur and other maps have been removed.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.6"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.6">v0.0.6</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Auto-strafe, CS-style knife holds and a calmer, juicier UI</h3><ul><li>Auto-strafe, a new style for anyone who doesn't want to tap A and D: in the air, just move the mouse and the game presses A or D for you, whichever way you turn. W does nothing in the air (it only slows you down there). Still your aim and your timing. Pick it in the map browser or the pause menu, or press F3.</li><li>Auto-strafe is its own mode: it has its own leaderboards, world records and rank, and doesn't count towards your overall rank, XP or map-clear achievements.</li><li>Auto-strafe runs don't add to the lifetime runs, jumps and time that achievements count, and #1 on the Auto-strafe rank doesn't earn the Style Champion title.</li><li>Steadier mouse look: the sudden flicks you never made, which some browsers send now and then with a fast mouse (1000 Hz and up, mostly when raw input is off or not supported), are filtered out, and so is the jump that could come right after you click into the game. Settings → Mouse &#38; view → Spike filter is on by default; it only drops a single mouse report far bigger than the ones around it, which no real flick is.</li><li>Settings → Mouse &#38; view → Show input stats (or ?inputdebug=1 in the address) shows, while you play: whether you have raw input, your mouse's polling rate, every movement, any flick the filter dropped, your frame times and stutters. Screenshot it when you report flicks or freezes; feedback sent with game info attached carries the same numbers.</li><li>Finishes are simpler: each one is a single design, the same for everyone. No more pattern numbers, fade percentages or Factory New; a finish's name is the whole story.</li><li>A new set of ten finishes, all our own: Sunset (a warm sky gradient with clouds, at level 20), Ember Glaze (a kiln-fired glaze, for 10,000 jumps), Tiger Lily (petal orange with dark freckles, for a tier 4+ map in another style), Nebula (gas clouds and twinkling stars, your first tier 4 map), Dewdrop Web (a silver web with dew, your first tier 5), Frost (ice and frost ferns, your first tier 6), Heartbeet (a sliced beetroot, for a world record), Four-Leaf (an emerald meadow of clovers, some of them gold, at level 50), plus Garden Fresh and Founder's Gold.</li><li>Nobody loses a finish: whatever you had equipped becomes its closest new look (Sunset Fade is now Sunset, Kiln Hardened is Ember Glaze, Doppelhop Phases 1, 2 and 4 and Black Pearl are Nebula, Sapphire and Phase 3 are Frost, Ruby is Heartbeet, Gamma Emerald is Four-Leaf, Bramble Web is Dewdrop Web), and anything you had earned the old way stays unlocked.</li><li>Unlocks, level-ups, achievements and rank-ups each get their own moment: one card at a time at the bottom of the screen, with the reward popping in, your level counting up and confetti for the big ones. They wait until your run is over, so nothing pops up in the middle of a run.</li><li>Meet the bunny: a little hooded bunny with a carrot now cheers your level-ups, shows off a rare finish, waves when you meet Huddled on a server, naps in an empty Inbox and looks sorry when a map won't load.</li><li>World and server records on the servers get a banner across the top (confetti for a world record, unless you're mid-run), and so does your own world record.</li><li>The end-of-run card lands with a little bounce, a new PB stamps onto it, and once your run is verified your points and XP count up and a top-10 place pops.</li><li>Small messages (link copied, sound off, now playing, stage splits, errors) look the same everywhere, stack neatly instead of covering each other, show ×2 when they repeat and stay while your mouse is over them. On a phone, swipe one away.</li><li>A new reply in your Inbox shows up as a message with an Open button, and the Inbox count pops when it goes up.</li><li>With reduced motion turned on in your system, all of this appears without animation.</li><li>The Loadout now lives in your profile: Profile → Loadout, next to Overview, Runs, Collection and Customise. The pause menu's Loadout button, Settings → Viewmodel and the Equip button on an unlock open it there directly. It's a normal page now with the knife big on the left and the items on the right, not a screen that covers everything.</li><li>Smooth scrolling and hovering in the profile and the Loadout, even on laptops: the blurred map behind full-screen menus is now a still picture instead of being redrawn and re-blurred every frame.</li><li>A shorter main menu that fits on every screen: Controls moved into Settings → Keys (&#34;How to bhop and every control&#34;), and Feedback and Inbox sit in one quiet row under your account.</li><li>The map browser's style picker is one row, so the style, its description and Play fit on screen together, from 720p up.</li><li>Long player names no longer disappear from leaderboard rows, the music's &#34;now playing&#34; note no longer covers the pause menu, and a sign-in message no longer hides behind an unlock.</li><li>Calmer menus: section labels are plain sentence-case text instead of small spaced-out capitals.</li><li>Knives are held the way CS holds them. The Bunnyfly idles open, blade forward like the CS butterfly knife, and its draw is the flip open (it only closes inside its inspect tricks). The Karrotbit hangs below your fist with the hook curving forward and away from you, ring on your index finger; turning it to face you is now how its inspect tricks end. Every knife idles in the same spot with or without the CS:S animations.</li><li>Better grips in every glove: your fingers wrap the handle and rest on it, with no gaps and no fingers sinking through it (the Carrot Blade's handle used to sit in your fingers rather than your fist), the thumb lies over your fingers below the guard, and the Daikon-tana's guard no longer cuts through your thumb. The Bunnyfly's fingers let go for its flips, and the wrist and sleeve cuff stay together when the hand bends.</li><li>A lower, smaller viewmodel by default: the knife sits low on the right and covers about as much of the screen as the CS:S knife does, with the blade in full view. If you never changed Settings → Viewmodel (FOV and offsets), you get the new look automatically; if you did, your settings are kept. Classic is the new default; Reset position goes back to it.</li><li>Five quiet new sounds go with the new messages: a soft tick when an Inbox message pops up, little rising ticks as your points and XP count up, a thump when a new PB stamps onto the end card, a tiny boing when the bunny hops, and a shimmer as a new finish or gloves shine. They play on the UI channel (Settings → Audio), sit well under the game, and never play mid-run.</li><li>Turn the keys overlay off (or back on) in one click: it's the first switch in Settings → HUD and in the pause menu's new On screen tab, next to switches for speed, timer, splits, sync, FPS, chat, name tags, ghosts and the viewmodel. You can also bind a key to it: Settings → Keys → Show / hide keys overlay (unbound to start with).</li><li>A shorter Settings page: what most people change comes first, small groups are merged, and what few people touch sits under Advanced at the end of its section (the spike filter and input stats, the rarer HUD elements, viewmodel offsets, bob and sway, channel mutes). Search still finds every setting and opens Advanced when the match is in there. Your settings carry over as they are.</li><li>Settings search knows more of the words players use (wasd, spike, flicks, loadout, viewmodel offset, hold to restart), and when nothing matches it suggests what you probably meant: Enter takes the suggestion.</li><li>Name tags over other players on a server can be turned off: Settings → Ghost → Player tags.</li><li>Fewer things blinking for attention: the &#34;new&#34; dots stay still, the green &#34;live&#34; dots are gone, the hop on the home screen plays once instead of looping, the pause menu shows one &#34;new&#34; mark at a time, and a few labels and key hints that said the same thing twice are gone.</li><li>The Loadout's first-person view shows your whole fist under the knife again with the new lower viewmodel.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.5"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.5">v0.0.5</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Knives, gloves, finishes and a smoother bhop</h3><ul><li>Knives, finishes and gloves. Every knife is yours to pick from the start; finishes and gloves unlock by playing.</li><li>A new Loadout screen (home menu, pause menu, or your profile under Customise): your hands holding the knife, big and live, with the whole blade in view. Hover any knife, finish or gloves to see it in your hands at once, click to equip. Switch to Close-up to turn the knife in the light by dragging, and Inspect (or F) plays its tricks.</li><li>Every item in the Loadout shows as itself, a little render of the knife in that finish or your hand in those gloves, with its rarity as a thin colour line. Locked ones say what unlocks them and how close you are, in one line. Arrow keys, Enter, Q / E and a controller all work there.</li><li>Sunset Fade: a carrot that fades from yellow through pink and purple to blue, unlocked at level 20.</li><li>More finishes with their own goals: Kiln Hardened for 10,000 jumps (Jackrabbit), Doppelhop Ruby for holding a world record, Doppelhop Sapphire for your first tier 6 map, Tiger Lily, Bramble Web, four Doppelhop phases, Black Pearl and Gamma Hop Emerald.</li><li>Every finish pattern is your own: no two players' Sunset Fades are quite the same. Customise shows your pattern number and, for Sunset Fade, how far your fade reaches.</li><li>Six knives next to the carrot: the Karrotbit (a hooked carrot karambit), the Bunnyfly balisong, the Daikon-tana, the Clover Cleaver, the Candy Cane Shiv and the Golden Carrot. More join as they are made.</li><li>Gloves: seven real styles, each with its own shape and materials, in 22 colourways, on your hands in first person and on your bunny. Sport (padded back panel, vented fingers, velcro strap), Driver (perforated leather with an open back and a snap), Hand Wraps (cloth wraps, bare fingertips, loose tails), Moto (hard knuckle plate, finger guards, long cuff), Specialist (tactical fingerless with a gauntlet cuff), Paw Pads (fuzzy, with toe beans and a paw print) and Garden (canvas with rubber-dipped tips). Stitching, leather grain, cloth weave and worn edges are all drawn live, no textures. Knit, the default, still follows your colourway.</li><li>Sport · Pandora is now plum and lilac with amber stitching, to sit better next to the bunny. Gloves you already had keep working.</li><li>Knives in other players' hands are about a third bigger, so you can tell a Karrotbit from a Cleaver at a glance.</li><li>The carrot grip is tidier: your thumb now rests along the handle under the guard instead of through it, and the Bunnyfly's handles no longer clip your thumb when it flicks open.</li><li>Other players on the servers see your knife, finish and gloves, and so do your replays and ghosts.</li><li>Each item has a rarity, from Garden to Golden. Unlocking a finish or gloves shows it off with an Equip button that opens the Loadout, and Settings → Viewmodel shows what you have equipped.</li><li>Hold the top of the rank board and it shows: overall #1, #2 and #3 wear a gold, silver or bronze crown on their bunny, on the servers, in replays and on their player card. Rank-only colourways (Reigning, Silver Hare, Bronze Hare), frames, trails and titles are yours for as long as you keep the place.</li><li>Leaderboards come in pages that fit your screen instead of a long scroll: page numbers, ← / → to flip (Page Up / Page Down in the pause menu), Jump to me, and a search to find any player's row. Map boards keep the world record pinned on every page and your own time below it, with each run's gap to the WR.</li><li>The rank board remembers its page and style in the address, so you can share a page, and shows how many points separate each player from the one above. Open any map's full leaderboard from its preview in the map browser.</li><li>Landing on a moving block (a door that sinks or slides when you touch it) no longer stops you dead now and then. On bhop_redwood it happened on the first few blocks from the start and sent your next hop out at about 30 u/s. Runs set before this fix keep their times, and their replays and ghosts play back exactly as they were run.</li><li>Maps no longer get stuck on the loading screen when a download stalls: it retries on its own, and if the map still can't load you get a Retry button instead of an endless wait.</li><li>The loading screen shows texture download progress, and on a slow connection you can skip the wait with Play without textures.</li><li>New option in Settings → Keys: Hold to restart. R, B and M then need a half-second hold, so a stray press can't end your run. Off by default.</li><li>New achievement, Play with the Owner: spend 30 seconds on the same server as Huddled, who made bunnyhop.lol, and it's yours, with the title &#34;Hopped with Huddled&#34;. It pops up in game the moment you earn it.</li><li>Staff tags on the servers: the owner's chat lines and scoreboard row carry an Owner tag, and server staff a Staff tag, so you know who is running the place. Their player cards show it too.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.4"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.4">v0.0.4</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>CS:S movement fixes, fixed maps and a new Settings page</h3><ul><li>Ducking in the air and landing no longer costs you speed: releasing crouch as you land still lets you jump right away, like in CS:S.</li><li>Player clips now block you like they do in CS:S. Some shortcuts through invisible walls no longer work.</li><li>Runs set before these movement changes keep their times, and their replays and ghosts play back exactly as they were run.</li><li>bhop_christmas and bhop_awful3 can be finished: their jump pad and floors are player clips, which you used to fall through. The same fix stops you dropping through the floor at teleport landings on about a dozen more maps.</li><li>bhop_alt_saimaa's jump pad launches you as high as it does in CS:S, high enough to reach the next level.</li><li>bhop_sharpie moves from tier 1 to tier 2.</li><li>New players start on bhop_ambience, a short and friendly tier 1 map, instead of bhop_eazy.</li><li>Settings is one page now: a sidebar with an icon per section jumps straight to Mouse &#38; view, Crosshair, HUD, Keys, Ghost, Graphics, Viewmodel, Audio or Account, and follows you as you scroll.</li><li>Search every setting with the words you'd actually use: sens, fov, crouch, autohop, carrot, name tags, fullscreen. Typos are fine. Press / to start typing, Enter jumps to the best match.</li><li>Every setting explains itself: a short line under its name, and an ⓘ with the details.</li><li>Take your setup anywhere: Export copies your settings as one code to paste in a chat, or saves them as a file. Import takes either one, tells you what changed, and has Undo.</li><li>Reset one section, or every setting at once, with a confirmation first.</li><li>Clearer controls: key binds look like keycaps, switches say On or Off, and every slider has a box for an exact number. Your current settings carry over as they are.</li><li>Crouching on Ctrl while you jump on the scroll wheel no longer zooms the page, and neither do Ctrl + plus, minus or 0 or a trackpad pinch while you play. Menus still zoom as usual.</li><li>Jumping on the scroll wheel while crouching on Shift works in every browser.</li><li>Some screens and glass on maps render correctly instead of as missing textures.</li><li>On the servers, type rtv, nominate, timeleft or nextmap in chat without the !, like on CS:S servers. &#34;nominate arcane&#34; nominates a map. Only the word on its own counts, so &#34;can we rtv&#34; stays a chat message.</li><li>kz maps are no longer in the server map rotation, and neither is bhop_caves_original. They are still in the map list to play on your own.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.3"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.3">v0.0.3</a></h2><span class="cl-kind major">Major</span><time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Real skies, fairer finishes, an inbox</h3><ul><li>The sky hides everything behind it, like in CS:S: no more seeing other stages through the sky on 65 maps.</li><li>3D skyboxes, with their fog, on 23 maps: bhop_japan's mountains, bhop_aztec's terrain and more.</li><li>Runs on bhop_monster_jam and bhop_kz_ravine count again. Their start zone sits above the floor, and those runs used to be rejected.</li><li>Runs on bhop_ananas, bhop_badges_ausbhop and the bhop_caves_original bonus are no longer rejected as out of sync.</li><li>End zones with a teleport on top of them finish your run: bhop_badges, bhop_fps_max_sr, bhop_noob and about 20 other maps finish more reliably.</li><li>Restarting on bhop_japan keeps you in the start zone, the same fix bhoptimer servers use.</li><li>Refreshed map thumbnails.</li><li>Send feedback from the game: Feedback on the home screen or in the pause menu, with an optional screenshot.</li><li>Save your progress with an email address. Sign in with a code or the link we send you.</li><li>The game goes fullscreen while you play. Turn it off under Settings → Graphics → Display.</li><li>Ctrl+W (crouch + forward) no longer closes the tab in Chrome and Edge. Other browsers ask before leaving the page mid-run.</li><li>Esc pauses and resumes reliably. If the browser won't give the mouse back, click to resume.</li><li>Replays open in first person.</li><li>An inbox. Replies to your feedback and announcements from bunnyhop.lol arrive in the game.</li><li>Name tags over other players are hidden behind walls now. A setting shows them through walls again if you prefer.</li><li>Move the carrot: X, Y and Z offset sliders under Settings → Viewmodel.</li><li>Menus and panels no longer overlap at small window sizes.</li><li>This changelog. The version in the corner of the home screen and the pause menu opens it, and bunnyhop.lol/changelog lists every version.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.2"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.2">v0.0.2</a></h2><span class="cl-kind minor">Minor</span><time datetime="2026-10-05">5 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>Stuck stages and faster loading</h3><ul><li>Fixed nine maps whose stage teleports never fired, so a fall left you stuck with the timer running: bhop_egyptiantemple, bhop_idiosyncrasy, bhop_forresttemple_beta, bhop_fuckfear_fix, bhop_christmas, bhop_japan, bhop_lego2, bhop_omniscient and bhop_strafe_fix.</li><li>Maps and textures load faster wherever you are: they are now cached close to you.</li></ul></article>
      <article class="cl-entry" id="v0.0.1"><div class="cl-meta"><h2><a href="#v0.0.1">v0.0.1</a></h2><span class="cl-kind major">Major</span><time datetime="2026-10-04">4 Oct 2026</time></div><h3>bunnyhop.lol launches</h3><ul><li>Classic Counter-Strike: Source bunnyhop in your browser. Real Source movement at 100 tick, nothing to install.</li><li>About 200 classic bhop maps from GameBanana, tiered T1 to T6, with bonus tracks and stage splits. Browse them by tier or by collection: Iconic, Short, Modern and the Prestige classics.</li><li>Five styles: Normal (autohop), Legit Scroll, W-Only, Sideways and Half-Sideways. Each has its own personal bests and leaderboards.</li><li>Verified leaderboards. Every run uploads a tick-exact replay, and the server plays it again before the time counts.</li><li>A replay of every finished run. Watch it in first person, chase, free, flyby or auto-director cameras, with a speed graph, and export it as an MP4 with the HUD, keys and sound.</li><li>Ghosts: race your PB, the world record or anyone's run from the leaderboard, with a live delta on the HUD.</li><li>Online servers, Easy (T1 to T3) and Hard (T4 to T6), with map votes, RTV, nominations, chat and spectating. Runs you finish online are verified like solo runs.</li><li>Profiles with points, ranks, levels and achievements, and cosmetics to unlock for your player card, ghost and trail.</li><li>The bunny, our own character, and its carrot blade in first person: Mouse 1 slashes, Mouse 2 stabs, F inspects.</li><li>Sound effects and music, a HUD you can lay out yourself, and every key rebindable.</li><li>Play as a guest from the first click. Link Discord to keep your progress on any device.</li></ul></article>
